{"posts":[{"id":"ftrretest_p3_51","t":"","a":"—","d":"","n":"#51","p":3,"im":["ea1e1e4c6d08c2d7db217c54d778034e794058f6"],"m":51},{"id":"ftrretest_p3_52","t":"Here is one that failed? I will have to look into this more.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#52","p":3,"im":["aab656652f67b0e8e4347dbd6264d624368fa513"],"m":52},{"id":"ftrretest_p3_53","t":"Mike1\n\nNot sure if I'm right, this is just my view, probably there were other causes beside these and in other TFs as well.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#53","p":3,"im":["34720c879edbb42f13e174c973101f842147e9bb"],"m":53},{"id":"ftrretest_p3_54","t":"rcmacf\n\nlivingdaylight wrote:\n\nSpot on, I reckon. I would be very careful with that one, on inspection, though, and wouldn't be surprised to see price drive a bit higher, and fake out into the area above.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#54","p":3,"im":["9f6c08fc83fe026e412223767c968dc239a749f8","4712c3ca20f8282de42fb6405cff8b4de576aa81","59d9dec5aa94752a8928a1bbeb376ff6e3a9a60c","3d2c5125557f75382ceed60a45aea3681571c246"],"m":54},{"id":"ftrretest_p3_55","t":"Mike1 wrote: Not sure if I'm right, this is just my view, probably there were other causes beside these and in other TFs as well.\n\nHuh? I guess I did not look at your FO comments that way. I was thinking of a FO along the lines of Peds. The main point to the FO is that it simply FO over that reaction to S/D. Maybe some others can chime in and help?","a":"—","d":"","n":"#55","p":3,"im":["34720c879edbb42f13e174c973101f842147e9bb"],"m":55},{"id":"ftrretest_p3_56","t":"4hr usdchf","a":"—","d":"","n":"#56","p":3,"im":["7e073e8e3a6a7c25586aec68607adb604c54c100"],"m":56},{"id":"ftrretest_p3_57","t":"","a":"—","d":"","n":"#57","p":3,"im":["7b29ad59a9c7fe3741d6990061af4816f6b2df92"],"m":57},{"id":"ftrretest_p3_58","t":"Price made a QM of of the top daily FTR and shot through the 4h FTR's right to the lower daily FTR on this 4h USDCHF chart","a":"—","d":"","n":"#58","p":3,"im":["1baa4546a70694de4d4cdec4cd2d2363972b0342"],"m":58},{"id":"ftrretest_p3_59","t":"Price is still bouncing between this FL and FTR. I am looking for it to ultimately overcome the FTR and challenge the price cap.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#59","p":3,"im":["4fec9b61126b314f770e20cfdfbff78c9d235f64"],"m":59},{"id":"ftrretest_p3_60","t":"The battle of FL vs FTR is over. 4h FTR moves to daily FTR on yen.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#60","p":3,"im":["8c82db5ba534cb3fa8e93e1d5247047b9f8f5a0e"],"m":60},{"id":"ftrretest_p3_61","t":"Wes\n\nI've edited my charts with paint, so the image obviously lost some quality\n\nI was doing some homework on price caps when I noticed something else on my charts. Well, at least I think I did. I'm new here, so I quite possibly could be wrong, but to me these are FTRs made after price broke minor resistance lines. Am I correct or am I horribly wrong?","a":"—","d":"","n":"#61","p":3,"im":["9588bd2cec6cda08fb48dc7494acb4dfc3001a00"],"m":61},{"id":"ftrretest_p3_62","t":"FTR,,please comments my chart","a":"—","d":"","n":"#62","p":3,"im":["17812a60207e692caac522f7b593d587634c1883","1fd49a4970d38087d279966a03fe75e26186790e"],"m":62},{"id":"ftrretest_p3_63","t":"Hi be70isme\n\nYour charts look good too me. As part of my learning I've added some comments and personal preference.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#63","p":3,"im":["34916d8e7e3b4d2abeb5762aba466c92d4984e30","0f62055d4270ba4184aafae0be741df92dc5a3d7"],"m":63},{"id":"ftrretest_p3_64","t":"JZ1986\n\nEURUSD H1 spotted a couple of important FTRs, I hope they're right J.Z\n\nsorry about the resolution","a":"—","d":"","n":"#64","p":3,"im":["ecaed1ed672e62284c299df2e97aba8181155462"],"m":64},{"id":"ftrretest_p3_65","t":"Mr.B\n\nJZ1986 wrote: EURUSD H1 spotted a couple of important FTRs, I hope they're right\n\nJ.Z\n\nThat fakeout you marked is a beautiful fakeout but why? Think about it from the IT's point of view. We have a defined S/R which is really obvious for everyone. When retail or the herd is short from that SR where would they probably have put their stops? (Think about it) IT's usually have 2 problems. First, they don't want retailers to follow them and second, they have massive amounts of orders to get filled for which they want the best possible price. Now when price shoots up what do you think retail would do? Price reaches your FTR and pins the S/R what orders would have been triggered? Fakeouts are there for a reason and they often spike to S/D or S/R. Just my thoughts.\n\nMr.B","a":"—","d":"","n":"#65","p":3,"im":["ecaed1ed672e62284c299df2e97aba8181155462","c37bccc8017ec26bdbb69809e185df8aca011f83"],"m":65},{"id":"ftrretest_p3_66","t":"JZ1986\n\nAbsolutely Mr. B:)","a":"—","d":"","n":"#66","p":3,"im":[],"m":66},{"id":"ftrretest_p3_67","t":"FTR trades.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#67","p":3,"im":["8d891d88f1903ddb541ee3644fb59f946fb27935"],"m":67},{"id":"ftrretest_p3_68","t":"","a":"—","d":"","n":"#68","p":3,"im":["c2405d05d8be6678e6be6815f30c04ef1f40d5fd"],"m":68},{"id":"ftrretest_p3_69","t":"1:3 RISK REWARD TRADE","a":"—","d":"","n":"#69","p":3,"im":["25beb87d99c27e963d7d338ee7fc4a0dfec5d4e1"],"m":69},{"id":"ftrretest_p3_70","t":"Hi Guys,\n\nI am trying to understand FTR`s now and I have one question. Is there a rule that FTR cannot be dip into some other PA pattern (most probably DBD,RBR)? Cause in present chart I found, that if FTR is created against gap, which was only half filled(pivot of FTR) bounce of it works great. It would be probably the same if it was created against continual small TF candle. Does it matter?","a":"—","d":"","n":"#70","p":3,"im":[],"m":70},{"id":"ftrretest_p3_71","t":"FTR in itself is a PA.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#71","p":3,"im":[],"m":71},{"id":"ftrretest_p3_72","t":"One more","a":"—","d":"","n":"#72","p":3,"im":["c2f2a72c4d51649d343d09c329751288a69f4b80"],"m":72},{"id":"ftrretest_p3_73","t":"bkumar\n\nHi,\n\nJust joined RTM a few days ago and already loving the information here. Engrossed over the last few days reading up stuff in the forum and videos. Though I have been in the markets for a while now, supply demand is an eye opener.\n\nHarsh, just a few observations on your chart and hope they are correct. Am sure you must have noticed them, But just that I was excited to spot them and hence sharing.\n\nCheers\n\nB.Kumar","a":"—","d":"","n":"#73","p":3,"im":[],"m":73},{"id":"ftrretest_p3_74","t":"bkumar\n\nHi,\n\nDon't know if my previous message was posted correctly. Hence trying again. Am new to RTM and still digesting the concepts. Spotted a few interesting things in your chart Harsh and thought of sharing it.\n\nAm sure you must have spotted them and it is just that I got excited and hence jotted a few things on your chart.\n\nCheers\n\nB.Kumar","a":"—","d":"","n":"#74","p":3,"im":["97070c22163e639a6aad6846785a0d9b1b9833fb"],"m":74},{"id":"ftrretest_p3_75","t":"bkumar\n\nHi Harshthakkar,\n\nJust my two cents observation. Please correct if there is any inconsistency as I am still new and learning RTM concepts.\n\nBest\n\nB.Kumar","a":"—","d":"","n":"#75","p":3,"im":["97070c22163e639a6aad6846785a0d9b1b9833fb"],"m":75}],"images":[{"k":"9f6c08fc83fe026e412223767c968dc239a749f8","t":"assets/thumbs/9f6c08fc83fe026e412223767c968dc239a749f8.webp","f":"assets/images/9f6c08fc83fe026e412223767c968dc239a749f8.jpeg","w":1500,"h":703,"b":56438,"o":"9f6c08fc83fe026e412223767c968dc239a749f8.jpeg","p":3,"pid":"ftrretest_p3_54"},{"k":"ea1e1e4c6d08c2d7db217c54d778034e794058f6","t":"assets/thumbs/ea1e1e4c6d08c2d7db217c54d778034e794058f6.webp","f":"assets/images/ea1e1e4c6d08c2d7db217c54d778034e794058f6.jpeg","w":1500,"h":394,"b":86365,"o":"ea1e1e4c6d08c2d7db217c54d778034e794058f6.jpeg","p":3,"pid":"ftrretest_p3_51"},{"k":"aab656652f67b0e8e4347dbd6264d624368fa513","t":"assets/thumbs/aab656652f67b0e8e4347dbd6264d624368fa513.webp","f":"assets/images/aab656652f67b0e8e4347dbd6264d624368fa513.png","w":1440,"h":900,"b":132783,"o":"aab656652f67b0e8e4347dbd6264d624368fa513.png","p":3,"pid":"ftrretest_p3_52"},{"k":"34720c879edbb42f13e174c973101f842147e9bb","t":"assets/thumbs/34720c879edbb42f13e174c973101f